 ### [DyNeRF](7274-dynerf.md)
-DyNeRF is a baseline method for representing volumetric videos by employing a single NeRF-like Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) that takes spatial coordinates and a temporal embedding as input to predict the radiance field for a specific video frame. It sets itself apart from its sibling [Neural Rendering of Variable Scenes](12734-neural-rendering-of-variable-scenes.md) by using a monolithic shared network structure rather than decomposing the scene into static and dynamic components or using explicit voxel structures. While simple to implement, this single shared MLP structure tends to lose details in high-frequency regions of the image.
