 ### [Explicit 4D Gaussian Splatting](14584-explicit-4d-gaussian-splatting.md)
-Explicit 4D Gaussian Splatting (Ex4DGS) is a method for dynamic novel view synthesis that achieves memory efficiency and rendering speed by separating scene primitives into static and dynamic categories and explicitly interpolating their attributes over time. Unlike implicit deformation fields or continuous trajectory models, Ex4DGS stores sparse keyframe data for dynamic Gaussians and uses specific interpolators to reconstruct continuous motion, handling complex phenomena like self-occlusion and object disappearance without requiring auxiliary masks or supervision. It builds on [Dynamic Scene Representation](15830-dynamic-scene-representation.md) by introducing a fully explicit temporal domain where attributes are sampled at discrete timestamps and interpolated.
