 ### [Gaussian Deformation Field (GauFRe)](15458-gaussian-deformation-field-gaufre.md)
-GauFRe is a dynamic scene representation that augments 3D Gaussian Splatting with a time-conditioned forward-warping deformation field to enable real-time novel view synthesis of dynamic scenes. Unlike NeRF-based methods that use backward warps to query canonical space, GauFRe stores Gaussians in a canonical space and uses a neural network to output deformed attributes (position, rotation, scale) for each time step $t$. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by explicitly separating the scene into static and deformable Gaussian sets, preventing capacity waste and noise in static regions, and by modeling non-rigid deformations (scaling) in addition to rigid motion.
